You manage to take long hand-made machete out of your backpack, like a comic book hero. You and your dad made this machete just for fun. Your father grumbled all the time, that such a knife is not a toy for kids. Probably, now he would be glad, that his present can save his son's life.
With a rapid stroke you cut the dreadful branch, and jump hastily out off the bush. Sticky branches shake, as if they were furious. Using the knife, you remove the branch that you had cut off from your hand with disgust. Just in time, because your skin starts burning.